            "review_title": "Review at Mai La Cafe",
            "review_text": "G C\nAnchorage, Alaska966 contributions\n0\nNice setting, polite & friendly service, good food\nMay 2015 • Solo\nThe Mai La Cafe is located in the Hoan Kiem District, and serves good Vietnamese food in a clean, well-decorated setting (with A/C). The staff are polite and friendly, and the dishes are served in nice sized portions, and items on their extensive menu seemed to be reasonably priced. My meal of grilled chicken with mushroom sauce came with a tender, juicy leg & thigh, vegetables, a big scoop of rice, and a fried egg (a full meal in itself)... I also ordered bitter melon stir fried with scrambled eggs, and this was tasty too. I will go back to try more of their offerings :)\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten May 23, 2015",
